{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04VB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$S^{-1}\\mathcal{C}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-right-localization}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6a7d0a9ec26060440f0b4bc961b10187c1ce41af8710c7eaeae155b441e30af2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:52ba56eec2441c5d5240a6c4d48a3550ff9e965ca78c674bfecdbb5bf1e6ba06", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category and let <MATH_0002> be a right multiplicative\nsystem.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The relation on pairs defined above is an equivalence relation.\n<STRUCT_0003> The composition rule given above is well defined on equivalence\nclasses.\n<STRUCT_0004> Composition is associative (and the identity morphisms satisfy\nthe identity axioms), and hence <MATH_0003> is a category.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:243f36bc651baef6bcf822094d53f78b59c0cf859e1852e70923e8b0b782118b", "unit_id": "tag:04VH:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04VB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-left-localization}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5013408880f92e2cd0bbf6a948ef0e9ea89deefc6618bdc338b552c96a97ac27", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:71aa1f793e20cfcb46b83e82d4fe973e2615de8541f87202058a21e79f91046a", "source_text": "This lemma is dual to\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nIt follows formally from that lemma by replacing\n<MATH_0001> by its opposite category in which\n<MATH_0002> is a left multiplicative system.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:29b811aebf00031ca5b7fbcaea49994f4d10f4609536d1a34b3d65a57cca824a", "unit_id": "tag:04VH:proof"}
